    <GaugingStation location="Iago flume" name="Iago" number="55035">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Rectangular, side contracted critical depth flume in IH/UKCEH research catchment. Natural flow regime. Discontinued in June 1999.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Shoal formation common, requiring prompt removal to avoid drowning. Gauged by c/m, and volumetrically at lowest flows.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Rectangular, side contracted critical depth flume designed by Hydraulics Research Ltd, suitable for streams with steep gradients, heavy sediment loads and high flood/drought flow ratios. Catchment nested within Cefn Brwyn (55008). Primary 15 minute dataset available.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Daily mean flows replaced from 01/10/1973 to 03/02/1999, and AMAXs flow from 01/10/1973 to 03/02/1999 following detailed QC (August 2025, WINFAP Files v14).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Responsive flow regime. Natural to within 10% at Q95.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Very wet catchment; drains Plynlimon massif. Composed of Ordovician grits, shales and slates and Silurian mudstones. Heath on peaty plateau; grassland on free draining slopes (supporting sheep grazing) and mires in valley bottoms.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">N</Comment>
        </Comments>
